1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,620
Real signals shake. We want the gentle shape underneath. A filter finds it.

2
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:13,020
Half of forty plus half of sixty is fifty. Averaging calms sudden jumps.

3
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:16,560
What's the average of 10, 20 and 90?

4
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:22,060
Your turn. Pause the video.

5
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:26,060
Forty. One wild number has less power when it shares.

6
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:32,470
Our filter looks at the latest eight samples. Each gets a weight. The middle ones

7
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:34,340
count most, the edges least.

8
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:41,392
Multiply, add them all, and you get one smoothed number. Then slide along by one and

9
00:00:41,392 --> 00:00:44,200
repeat. This is called a FIR filter.

10
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,220
Each weighted spot is a tap.

11
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:52,034
Slow changes survive. Fast wiggles fade. That's a low-pass filter. This one is

12
00:00:52,034 --> 00:00:55,860
designed to start fading things around 500 wiggles per second.

13
00:00:56,860 --> 00:01:06,673
Our chip has no special hardware for decimals. So each weight is multiplied by

14
00:01:06,673 --> 00:01:11,580
32,768 and rounded. This is called Q15.

15
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:20,514
After adding everything, we divide by 32,768 once, by shifting fifteen places. All

16
00:01:20,514 --> 00:01:27,920
eight weights add to exactly 32,768, so a steady signal keeps its level.

17
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:34,052
The first samples of a new basket need the last seven from the old one. We save

18
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:36,520
them, so there's no bump at each swap.

19
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:41,840
Smoothing looks at the past, so the smooth line arrives a little late.

20
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:48,199
Ten thousand lines a second won't fit down our message cable. So we print every

21
00:01:48,199 --> 00:01:51,320
sixteenth sample, while filtering all of them.

22
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:55,980
This thinning is called decimation. Let's build it.

